rful stunts and from the second  helmet took nothing because the second  films suck you adding a really awesome  female character Tom Cruise still being  really good at doing this stuff Simon  Pegg being fun the action being well  shot and yeah this was just  well-executed adrenaline number six  Kingsman the Secret Service boy did this  one come out of nowhere it was kind of  on my radar because I really like the  director Matthew Vaughn he hasn't made a  bad movie yet and this just this is  james bond for the new generation and  and it's violent and it's funny and it's  vicious in its clever and it's  self-aware and a very unpretentious way  in the performances  all gray mica colin firth is an action  star who knew the main character is well  he was really good and and actually all  the young actors were really good in  Samuel Jackson was a little bit off but  in a really intriguing and fun way  everyone just seemed to really just be  having so much fun making this film and  it's one of those things where the fun  that they are having bleeds out and you  just get that same feeling watching it  and the fact that it's well executed on  top of all that yeah this is just a  great time number 5 inside out this is  pics are doing what they do best taking  an interesting idea and just diving into  it the best way that it can be done just  the little voices inside your head the  different emotions that you feel who's  in control who doesn't get along how  does the inside of your brain work not  on any sort of actual legitimate  neurological sense but like in a sort of  a psychological examination way and it's  really fun and it's really clever and  yeah yeah I'd teared up at a few point  if you've seen the movie you know what  part it was yeah yeah I did but you did  too don't you lie number for ex machina  I just really love the way this film  examined its questions of identity and  what it means to be human what it means  to be enslaved what it means to have  rights what